1
00:12:37,894 --> 00:12:43,894
The Search for Alexander the Great is a documentary,
history, tv movie film directed by Peter Sykes.

2
00:25:15,789 --> 00:25:21,789
Friends, contemporaries and even enemies of Alexander the Great
gather in a tent to tell his tale through their eyes.

3
00:37:53,684 --> 00:37:59,684
Narrator, played by James Mason.

4
00:50:31,578 --> 00:50:37,578
Olympias, played by Jane Lapotaire.

5
01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
Darius of Persia, played by Robert Stephens.

6
01:15:47,368 --> 01:15:53,368
Philip II, played by Julian Glover.

7
01:28:25,263 --> 01:28:31,263
Alexander, played by Nicholas Clay.

8
01:41:03,157 --> 01:41:09,157
Hephaistion, played by Ian Charleson.

9
01:53:41,052 --> 01:53:47,052
The Burning (aka Carnage) is a 1981 Canadian-American slasher film directed by Tony Maylam, and
starring Brian Matthews, Leah Ayres, Brian Backer, Larry Joshua, and Lou David.

10
02:06:18,947 --> 02:06:24,947
Its plot follows a summer camp caretaker who is horribly burnt from a prank gone
wrong, where he seeks vengeance at a nearby summer camp years later.

11
02:18:56,842 --> 02:19:02,842
The film marks the debuts of actors Jason Alexander,
Fisher Stevens, and Holly Hunter.

12
02:31:34,736 --> 02:31:40,736
The film is an international co-production between the United States and Canada.

13
02:44:12,631 --> 02:44:18,631
Based on the New York urban legend of the Cropsey maniac, the screenplay was written by Bob Weinstein and
Peter Lawrence, from a story conceived by producer Harvey Weinstein, Tony Maylam, and Brad Grey.

14
02:56:50,526 --> 02:56:56,526
Rick Wakeman, of the progressive rock band Yes, composed the score.

15
03:09:28,421 --> 03:09:34,421
The Burning was theatrically released on May 8, 1981, by Filmways.

16
03:22:06,315 --> 03:22:12,315
Its critical reception was largely unfavorable, with many film critics deriding its
similarities to Friday the 13th and Friday the 13th Part 2 and its graphic violence.

17
03:34:44,210 --> 03:34:50,210
However, it has since become a cult classic and received
positive reappraisal from film critics.

18
03:47:22,105 --> 03:47:28,105
The film explores themes of aristotle, alexander the great,
ancient greece, 4th century bc, documentary.
